## 16. Milestone M8 — Windows launcher and baseline quality

Owner decision October10, 2026: implement the working internal launcher first,
with a named library of selectable personal save directories independent of
builds. Then fix baseline Windows problems, including those on the RTX5060.
Stock and a validated 60 FPS mode are in scope; all modes above60, dynamic/VRR
and uncapped capability expansion are later milestones. This supersedes the
earlier broad enhancement/platform roadmap without promoting old experiments.
[Scope, execution order and data boundaries](docs/M8-priorities.md).

**Goal:** a practical Windows testing build with isolated personal data, honest
settings, baseline bug fixes and correct optional60 behavior. No full campaign,
unlock grind, release-ready installer or secondary-platform promise.

**Estimate:** re-estimate after external-root/launcher foundation and measured
baseline triage; no inherited 2–10-week platform estimate or FPS guarantee.

